From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Taylor <miketaylr@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:11:52 -0700
Subject: Treat ORB-blocked media responses as CORS cross-origin

When a no-cors media request is blocked by ORB, the load fails with
net::ERR_BLOCKED_BY_ORB and goes through
ResourceMultiBufferDataProvider::DidFail() rather than
DidReceiveResponse(). Only DidReceiveResponse() records whether the
response is CORS cross-origin, so ORB-blocked loads were never marked
as such.

As a result, HTMLMediaElement handled these failures differently from
other cross-origin load failures (e.g. reporting a different
MediaError message).

Mark the UrlData as CORS cross-origin in DidFail() when the error is
ERR_BLOCKED_BY_ORB, since ORB only applies to cross-origin no-cors
responses. This makes http/tests/media/media-load-nonmedia-crossorigin.html
pass consistently, so remove its TestExpectations entry.

Bug: 40257965
Change-Id: Ia39a3d1cdc40e942d7ff50b0b1a42910dd06acc4
